<title>USA: Key Energy buys well services firm.</title>
<headline>Key Energy buys well services firm.</headline>
<dateline>EAST BRUNSWICK, N.J. 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Key Energy Group Inc said on Friday that it has agreed to acquire the trucking and well service assets of an undisclosed Oklahoma company for $2.7 million.</p>
<p>The assets acquired include three well service rigs, 21 trucks, 32 trailers, 40 frac tanks, construction equipment, vehicles and two saltwater disposal wells, Key Energy said.</p>
<p>The acquired assets will be operated by Key Energy's WellTech MidContinent division, the company said.</p>
